## Step 5: Register the Service in AOT (Service Node Configuration)

```xpp
/// <summary>
/// Service Registration - Add to AOT > Services Node
/// This is configured via metadata in Visual Studio (AOT)
/// Below shows the service attributes applied to the class
/// </summary>

// Apply these attributes to your Service Class for proper registration
[
    SysEntryPointAttribute(true),
    AifServiceOperationActionAttribute('getCustomer',     AifServiceOperationAction::Read),
    AifServiceOperationActionAttribute('getAllCustomers',  AifServiceOperationAction::Read),
    AifServiceOperationActionAttribute('createCustomer',  AifServiceOperationAction::Create),
    AifServiceOperationActionAttribute('updateCustomer',  AifServiceOperationAction::Update),
    AifServiceOperationActionAttribute('deleteCustomer',  AifServiceOperationAction::Delete)
]
public class CustomerRESTService
{
    // Service methods defined above...
}
```

---

## Step 6: Create a Custom Service Group

```xml
<!-- 
    AOT > Service Groups > New Service Group
    Name: CustomerServiceGroup
    Add your service: CustomerRESTService

    This is done via Visual Studio AOT, 
    below is the conceptual XML representation
-->
<ServiceGroup>
    <Name>CustomerServiceGroup</Name>
    <Services>
        <Service>
            <Name>CustomerRESTService</Name>
            <ServiceClass>CustomerRESTService</ServiceClass>
            <Operations>
                <Operation>getCustomer</Operation>
                <Operation>getAllCustomers</Operation>
                <Operation>createCustomer</Operation>
                <Operation>updateCustomer</Operation>
                <Operation>deleteCustomer</Operation>
            </Operations>
        </Service>
    </Services>
</ServiceGroup>
```

---

## Step 7: Consuming the REST Service

```http
### Authenticate - Get Token
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant-id}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials
&client_id={client-id}
&client_secret={client-secret}
&resource=https://{d365-environment}.dynamics.com

---

### GET - Retrieve Single Customer
GET https://{environment}.dynamics.com/api/services/CustomerServiceGroup/CustomerRESTService/getCustomer?_custAccount=US-001
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
Content-Type: application/json

---

### GET - Retrieve All Customers
GET https://{environment}.dynamics.com/api/services/CustomerServiceGroup/CustomerRESTService/getAllCustomers
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
Content-Type: application/json

---

### POST - Create Customer
POST https://{environment}.dynamics.com/api/services/CustomerServiceGroup/CustomerRESTService/createCustomer
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "_contract": {
        "CustName"  : "New Customer Inc.",
        "CustGroup" : "10",
        "Currency"  : "USD",
        "IsActive"  : true
    }
}

---

### POST - Update Customer
POST https://{environment}.dynamics.com/api/services/CustomerServiceGroup/CustomerRESTService/updateCustomer
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "_contract": {
        "CustAccount" : "US-001",
        "CustGroup"   : "20",
        "Currency"    : "EUR"
    }
}

---

### POST - Delete Customer
POST https://{environment}.dynamics.com/api/services/CustomerServiceGroup/CustomerRESTService/deleteCustomer
Authorization: Bearer {access_token}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "_custAccount": "US-001"
}
```

---

## Step 8: Security Setup

```xpp
/// <summary>
/// Create a Security Privilege for the Service
/// Apply this to your service methods via AOT Security
/// </summary>

// AOT > Security > Privileges > New Privilege
// Name: CustomerRESTServicePrivilege

// Then create a Duty and Role and assign accordingly
// This is typically done through AOT metadata

// Example Security Attribute on Service Method:
[SysEntryPointAttribute(true)]
public CustomerServiceContract getCustomer(str _custAccount)
{
    // D365 will automatically check user permissions
    // based on the security configured in AOT
}
```

---

## Project Structure Summary

```
📁 Solution
 ├── 📁 Data Contracts
 │    ├── 📄 CustomerServiceContract.xpp
 │    ├── 📄 CustomerServiceResponse.xpp
 │    └── 📄 CustomerListResponse.xpp
 │
 ├── 📁 Services
 │    └── 📄 CustomerRESTService.xpp
 │
 ├── 📁 Service Groups (AOT Metadata)
 │    └── 📄 CustomerServiceGroup
 │
 └── 📁 Security
      ├── 📄 CustomerRESTServicePrivilege
      ├── 📄 CustomerRESTServiceDuty
      └── 📄 CustomerRESTServiceRole
```

---

## Key Points

| Component | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `[DataContractAttribute]` | Marks class as serializable for service |
| `[DataMemberAttribute]` | Maps class property to JSON field |
| `[SysEntryPointAttribute]` | Marks method as service entry point |
| `ttsbegin/ttscommit` | Transaction management |
| `Service Group` | Groups services for REST endpoint exposure |
| `OAuth 2.0` | Authentication mechanism for API calls |

> **Note:** After deployment, the service is automatically available at:
> `https://{environment}.dynamics.com/api/services/{ServiceGroup}/{ServiceClass}/{Method}`

